4. Required fixes (the deliverable)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ordered by priority. F10 is the gate: nothing else can be hardware-validated
until it lands. Repo column: where the fix lives (clustervision repos are STAGED
locally + documented for a human MR, not pushed — repo-scope rule).

PRIORITY 0 — make legacy runnable again  [DONE — implemented + deployed]
  F10 [A, BLOCKER]  luna2-daemon.  install_mode=legacy must select the legacy
      install template instead of the lpart-pipeline one. IMPLEMENTED as a NAMING
      convention (the original name is reserved for legacy; the lpart pipeline gets
      its own name), reusing the per-method-template machinery
      (daemon/base/boot.py:1362-1363; templ_install_kickstart.cfg precedent):
        (a) RENAME daemon/templates/templ_install.cfg -> templ_install_lpart.cfg
            (the v1.4 lpart pipeline, unchanged content).
        (b) ADD daemon/templates/templ_install.cfg = the LEGACY/original template:
            prescript/partscript/postscript run `customscript <stage>` (skipping
            the node FIELD when it is the lpart thin shim, via `grep -q
            lpart-node-installer`), and the image is laid down by the template's own
            restored unpack_imagefile + download_image (NOT lpart-osimage-install).
            No /lunatmp/skip_unpack drop, no TUI.
        (c) boot.py install() lever: default (no-method) path routes by
            install_mode — legacy -> templ_install.cfg; everything else ->
            templ_install_lpart.cfg. (install_mode is already in the node data.)
      Net: in legacy the node never invokes lpart-node-installer; it runs the old
      prescript/partscript/postscript + unpack, exactly as pre-lpart Luna did. The
      client guard (decide.go:21) then correctly never sees legacy.
      STATUS: staged at /root/luna2-v1.4-patches/legacy + deployed on this
      controller; both renders verified; legacy diskfull HW-validated (boots).
      ALT (if legacy is being retired): instead reject install_mode=legacy at the
      luna CLI / daemon with a clear message ("legacy unsupported on lpart clients")
      rather than letting it fail opaquely at the partscript. Either way the
      current silent "Part script exited with exit code 1" must go.
      Client-side (THIS repo, optional hardening): lpart-storage-prepare/decide.go
      could emit a louder, actionable error naming the daemon-template fix, so a
      mis-served legacy node fails with a diagnosis, not a bare refusal.

PRIORITY 1 — raid1 HA correctness (once F10 lets it run)
  F1 [B, BLOCKER]  luna2-daemon raid1.py: mirror ESP(p1)+boot(p2) as metadata-1.0
      md arrays (md-efi/md-boot), write both ESPs, fstab the md — so either leg
      boots alone. Model: the new installer's BootMirrorDevice (and the doc's own
      commented md0/md1/md2 example). Without it, losing disk1 = unbootable.
  F6 [B, BLOCKER]  raid1.py: zero+wipefs each md member before `mdadm --create`,
      and write `AUTO -all` early in the partscript (the legacy initramfs has no
      such guard — A1), so a re-run over stale superblocks is deterministic.

PRIORITY 2 — UEFI/ESP hygiene (all disk plugins)
  F3  mkfs.fat -F 32 (not -F 16) for the ESP.            diskfull/raid1/nodhcp
  F4  parted: `name 1 "EFI System Partition"` (add space). diskfull/nodhcp
  F5  `set 1 boot on` (ESP), not `set 2`.                 diskfull/nodhcp

PRIORITY 3 — fstab robustness / docs
  F7  nodhcp: fstab by UUID, not /dev/sdaN.               luna2-daemon nodhcp.py
  F9  cloud post.rd: fstab root by UUID, not device name. trinityx-combined
  F2  howto raid1 inspiration: fix /dev/${DISK}p1 -> ${DISK}1 (or delete the
