############################################################################

F11 [A, BLOCKER — supersedes F10's root cause]  legacy lever works, but its
    shim-skip regex is stale after the tx->lpart rename.
    CONFIRMED ON HARDWARE (node001, 2026-06-07 PM, diskfull re-run):
      * F10's fix (the install_mode legacy lever in base/boot.py + a legacy
        templ_install.cfg whose pre/part/post SKIP the lpart thin-shim FIELD and
        run customscript instead) IS deployed live and the lever DOES serve
        templ_install.cfg for install_mode=legacy. So F10's stated root cause
        ("legacy routing missing") is no longer the issue.
      * BUT the shim-skip guard greps the PRE-RENAME marker:
            grep -qE 'tx-node-installer|lpart-node-installer' /lunatmp/<stage>script.sh
        The GLOBAL RENAME changed the thin shim to `exec /usr/bin/lpart-phase
        <stage>`, which matches NEITHER alternative. Verified: the guard prints
        "legacy mode -- skipping ..." when it fires; the 16:04-16:09 retry cycles
        on node001 show ZERO such lines (the 6 in history are pre-rename). Direct
        check: `printf 'exec /usr/bin/lpart-phase part' | grep -qE
        'tx-node-installer|lpart-node-installer'` -> NO MATCH.
      * Net: guard never skips -> the lpart-phase shim runs under legacy ->
        lpart-storage-prepare hits decide.go:21 ("install_mode=legacy is
        daemon-only and must not reach the client") -> exit 1 -> "Part script
        exited with exit code 1. Stop install." -> luna2-start.sh retries the
        same un-retryable failure forever. This is also why the operator saw the
        TUI in legacy mode at all.
    ROOT CAUSE: one stale regex in templ_install.cfg (3 occurrences). The rename
    updated the shims and the client but not the legacy template's shim detector.
    FIX (staged at /root/luna2-v1.4-patches/legacy, NOT pushed — clustervision):
      (A) templ_install.cfg: add `|lpart-phase` to the 3 shim-skip greps. With the
          shim skipped, legacy runs ONLY customscript (the --scripts plugin): no
          lpart, no TUI -- "legacy means legacy". [APPLIED in the staged copy.]
      (B) both templates: `exit 1` -> `exit $LUNARET` in the pre/part/post
          handlers, so install.sh propagates a fatal exit code. [Specified in the
          staged README; deliberately left for the human MR.]
    CLIENT-SIDE (luna2-client, branch advanced-partitioner — DONE, make check green):
      * lpart-node-installer refuses install_mode=legacy at startup: plain console
        FATAL, NO TUI, NO pipeline, exit code 3 (exitFatalConfig). Reads the
        daemon-written install-context.json (installcontext.LoadFile). Backstop so
        a mis-served legacy node fails plainly instead of in a buried TUI error.
        (cmd/lpart-node-installer/main.go + main_test.go TestLegacyRefusal.)
      * luna2-start.sh (redhat/x86): captures install.sh's real exit code and, on
        the fatal sentinel (3), parks in a maintenance shell (fatal_park) instead
        of the retry_countdown loop. Needs daemon fix (B) to receive the 3.
    STATUS: campaign still BLOCKED on hardware until fix (A) is deployed to the
    live daemon (or the node's shim overrides are cleared). node001 left at its
    healthy auto baseline.
